  "goodToKnow": "Die Heide is heathland, open sandy land covered in heather (das Heidekraut). The best known is the Lüneburger Heide south of Hamburg, which turns purple in August and is famous for its Heidschnucken sheep and Heidehonig. With a different gender, der Heide (die Heidin) means a heathen or pagan, and das Heidentum is paganism. Heidenangst and Heidenlärm, though, simply mean a huge fright and a terrible racket."
